    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded by African American settlers, Liberia became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>’s first republic on 26 July 1847.</li><li>With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, it was one of only two African states to escape European colonisation during the partition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</li><li>A settler elite ruled until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-doe">Samuel Doe</a>’s coup in 1980, which was followed by civil wars from 1989 to 2003.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Liberia runs one of the world’s largest ship registries: thousands of foreign-owned merchant ships sail under its flag of convenience, a system set up in 1948.</p></aside>
    </section>

